process-spawn-at.m's process kind spawned on the machine's GPU
(docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU processes without omp target, step 4c): the runtime
loads the module's image through liboffload, sets its device number, and
launches the kind's kernel, which receives the host's messages through its
mailbox's ring and sends its answer back. The program ends when main does,
even while a GPU process waits for messages. A program compiled for another
GPU has no image for this one, which is a software error at the spawn.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-spawn-at.m -o %t2
RUN: %libomp-env %t2 gpu | FileCheck %S/process-spawn-at.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: merkc -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-spawn-at.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env %t gpu | FileCheck %S/process-spawn-at.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: %libomp-env %t2 leave | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEAVE --match-full-lines
LEAVE:main ends

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=gfx906 %libomp-flags %S/process-spawn-at.m -o %t.other
RUN: not %libomp-env %t.other gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OTHER
OTHER: Software Error: process_spawn_at.spawn_summer_at: the module process_spawn_at has no image of its GPU process kinds for GPU 0, a {{gfx[0-9a-f]+}}: it must be compiled with --offload-arch={{gfx[0-9a-f]+}}

The messages that the GPU process took from its ring are freed.
RUN: %libomp-env MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MESSAGES --match-full-lines
MESSAGES:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
